    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d614">

                <pb facs="0593" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 337.11/465</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>United Fruit Company report to Department that 2,000 rebels have camped on the
                    borders of their property and seem to be in aggressive mood.</p>
                <pb facs="0594" n="428" xml:id="pg428"/>
                <p>You are instructed to inform the Cuban Government of the foregoing and request
                    that such troops as may be necessary be sent to the location for its proper
                    protection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
